.TH ASGARD-SETUP 1 "November 2026" "bifrost-emu 2.0.0-beta.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asgard-setup \- install Asgard, the Android layer of bifrost-emu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B asgard-setup
[\fB\-\-system\fR | \fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIDIR\fR | \fB\-\-uninstall\fR | \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR | \fB\-\-verify\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Downloads the pinned Android pieces (the Bionic runtime, an Android 15 system image of 734 MiB for ART, the
framework and media libraries, the signing tools and microG; about 1.5 GB in all, each checked by hash), builds
the adapters and launcher, and installs Asgard (about 1.1 GB) under \fI~/.local\fR. It needs several GB of free
disk space while it runs and keeps its working copy in \fI~/.cache/bifrost/setup\fR.
.PP
Afterwards \fBbifrost-emu\fR \fIapp.apk\fR installs and runs an Android app from any directory. Android windows need
libsdl3\-0 3.2 or newer.
.SH OPTIONS
The options are those of install\-asgard.py: \fB\-\-system\fR installs under /usr/local (needs root), \fB\-\-prefix\fR
\fIDIR\fR under DIR, \fB\-\-uninstall\fR removes an install, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR lists what would change and
\fB\-\-verify\fR compares file contents.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bifrost-emu (1)
